> Just drop your sack when you see a monster and maybe retreat to a
> doorway. They *never* loot sacks/bags/chests/boxes.

Risky.  If you're levitating, say bye-bye to all the breakables in the
bag (had that happen once when I decided I needed to run away faster
on Medusa); and, as you note elsewhere, there are monsters that can
eat bags & boxes that are laying around (again, I've had a gel cube
eat a dropped BoH...and then struggled along bagless until I found a
BoH in Orcus town; the RNG was being stingy).  The only safe spot to
drop your loot/emergency supplies is on a burned-in E (with a cursed
item on top if you've got strong pets).

Far better, in my opinion, is to play on a system with menu colors
enabled (NAO does), and set your config so that all risky items (BoH/
BoT/#named wands/etc.) are highlighted, giving you a reminder that you
need to be careful.

